  "note": "Presentation only (X33 · M7). The field is the simulator's own lattice: engine.json `road` holds one settlement per cell in axial coordinates measured from the starting settlement, and this file names the cells they land on. A cell id (row letter A-O plus column number 1-20) is a reference mark drawn on the sheet, never a position the simulation reads. What the sheet draws: every cell of the field, the terrain a cell stands on, the settlement mark on its own cell, one named sub-zone cell and one named wild cell per side of a town, the walk graph between settlements, the landmark marks, the region names and the travel pin. Nothing here carries a level band, a sub-zone name or a race — those are the engine's, printed into the cells by tools/map.ts, so the sheet and the content cannot disagree. A wild cell is a side of a town with no sub-zone on it yet: it is named after the town it rings and holds no content of its own until one is written.",
